@startuml
actor Curator
participant "Web / HTTP" as Web
participant "RC application" as App
participant "Authority Management" as AM
participant "RC domain" as Domain
database "RC repository" as Repo

== Resource mutation ==
Curator -> Web : submit authenticated mutation
Web -> App : command + server actor context
App -> AM : admit CurateResourceCatalogue\n@ resource-catalogue
alt denied or unknown
  AM --> App : denial / ambiguity
  App --> Web : public failure; no mutation
else admitted
  AM --> App : admitted
  App -> Domain : apply accepted command/invariants
  Domain --> App : domain result
  App -> Repo : persist RC transaction
  Repo --> App : committed result
  App --> Web : command result / projection
end

== Address replacement ==
Curator -> Web : replacement + expectedVersion
Web -> App : selected fact + temporal input
App -> AM : admission
AM --> App : admitted
App -> Domain : validate current fact/version/time
Domain --> App : end current + successor semantics
App -> Repo : atomic RC persistence
Repo --> App : updated projection
App --> Web : replacement result

== Workspace read ==
Curator -> Web : resource workspace query + asOf
Web -> App : paging/search/filter request
App -> Repo : load Resource + effective RC facts
Repo --> App : RC-owned facts
App --> Web : projection with explicit missing facts

note over App,AM
responsibilityScope is business-data filtering.
It is not substituted for the fixed
Resource Catalogue authority scope.
end note

note over Web,Repo
This pilot documents architecture only.
Product code and tests are not modified.
end note

@enduml